4. Current work and future challenges

Figure 7: phishing activity of 2020

A phishing site attack is still regarded as an appealing method of persuading an inexperienced internet user to give the attackers his or her private confidential information. There are various measures available, but once a solution is suggested to counter these attacks, phishers consider the solution's vulnerabilities and continue their attacks. Several anti-phishing solutions have been proposed in the past. The majority of jobs, whether in government or industry, educational programmes, companies, and non-commercial activities have moved online.

